  "content": {
    "id": "p11-ch17-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "The product of a number and four less than the number is equal to 16 more than twice the number. Find the number.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$-2$ or $8$.",
      "worked": "Let the number be $x$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x(x-4)&=2x+16\\\\x^2-4x&=2x+16\\\\x^2-6x-16&=0\\\\(x-8)(x+2)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nBy the null factor law, $x-8=0$ or $x+2=0$, so $x=8$ or $x=-2$.\n\nCheck: $8(8-4)=32=16+2(8)$ and $(-2)(-2-4)=12=16+2(-2)$. Both numbers satisfy the statement.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 51
  },
